 "notes": {
  "7163:1631": "pain: she is visibly ill, eyes shut, sneezing; a learner could read suffering/pain into being sick",
  "7216:3680": "acknowledge: the driver leans out and waves her mitten at the helper, which reads as acknowledging/thanking him",
  "8:5211": "front door: she taps the card on a door and opens the door to her room; a learner may accept front door for the room entrance door",
  "7802:3730": "assault: the scene is an obstacle race with climbing wall and mud, i.e. an assault course in British usage",
  "4447:1425": "heat: the last shot is a warm pub with a hot cup of tea",
  "4022:1757": "road: the plane flies over a city with rows of houses below, so roads are plausibly visible",
  "553:16": "athletics: stadium with players training; athletics in the American sense means sports in general",
  "4797:2176": "yellow: a block of hard cheese is normally pale yellow even though the pile is described as white",
  "4485:1437": "hill: the lake is ringed by snowy peaks; hill is a near neighbour of mountain",
  "7323:2131": "watch: bare word also reads as the verb; the man stands in the doorway looking on at the bed-making"
 }
